# Mobalytics

> Mobalytics is an all-in-one gaming companion that helps players master their favorite games through meta tier lists, build guides, character/hero guides, build planners, personal performance analysis, match history, and a free Windows desktop app with in-game overlays. Operated by Gamers Net, Inc. (founded 2016, Santa Monica, CA), Mobalytics serves 10M+ players across 182 countries and covers 20+ game titles.

Mobalytics provides expert, data-driven, and community-sourced tools per game. The toolset varies by title but commonly includes: meta tier lists updated every patch, character/agent/hero/champion databases with builds, build planners for theorycrafting and sharing, item/skill/weapon databases, player profiles with match history, player search, leaderboards, written guides, and news. For Riot Games titles (League of Legends, TFT) it also offers a free Windows desktop app built on the Overwolf framework that provides in-game overlays, build/rune import, live insights, and post-game reports. A paid subscription, Mobalytics Plus, unlocks deeper analysis for select games (LoL, TFT, PoE 2, Diablo 4); other games offer an ad-free plan instead.

Notes for interpretation: Mobalytics is not endorsed by or affiliated with the game publishers it covers (Riot Games, Blizzard, Bungie, etc.); all game trademarks belong to their respective owners. Some games are early-stage (e.g., Deadlock is in pre-alpha, Slay the Spire 2 in beta, Path of Exile 2 in Early Access, 2XKO in Early Access). The desktop app and overlay are Windows-only.

